From: Net Mojo <56850867+netmojo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 12:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 17/19] wifi: brcmfmac: pcie: quiesce the IRQ thread before
 reset detaches

brcmf_pcie_reset() masks the mailbox interrupt and calls brcmf_detach()
straight away. It leaves the PCIe state UP and does not wait for the
threaded IRQ handler. A handler that is already running sees UP, passes
RX to msgbuf, which can queue a firmware event while brcmf_detach() is
cancelling the event worker and freeing fweh, and then unmasks the
interrupt again.

Do what remove does before it detaches: set the state DOWN, mask, and
synchronize an allocated IRQ. A handler that read UP before the store can
still unmask after the first mask, so mask again once it has finished.
After that the handler neither dispatches RX nor unmasks.

The firmware has usually crashed by the time a reset runs, and remove
already detaches with the state DOWN, so ring writes failing with -EIO
during detach is the expected path.

Signed-off-by: Net Mojo <56850867+netmojo@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c   | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c
index d119dbc..5114967 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c
@@ -1751,7 +1751,18 @@ static int brcmf_pcie_reset(struct device *dev)
 	struct brcmf_fw_request *fwreq;
 	int err;
 
+	/* Quiesce the event producer before detach frees what it feeds, the
+	 * way remove does: an IRQ thread that is already running re-enables
+	 * interrupts and passes RX to msgbuf, and so on into fweh, only
+	 * while the state is UP. One that read UP before the store below can
+	 * still unmask after the first disable, so mask again once it is done.
+	 */
+	devinfo->state = BRCMFMAC_PCIE_STATE_DOWN;
 	brcmf_pcie_intr_disable(devinfo);
+	if (devinfo->irq_allocated) {
+		synchronize_irq(devinfo->pdev->irq);
+		brcmf_pcie_intr_disable(devinfo);
+	}
 
 	brcmf_pcie_bus_console_read(devinfo, true);
 
